  "content": {
    "title": "Will Smith, Andy Pages homer as Dodgers beat Diamondbacks on Opening Day",
    "text": "Updated March 26, 2026, 11:30 p.m. ETThe Los Angeles Dodgers rallied with success in the middle innings to beat the Arizona Diamondbacks, 8-2, in the season opener at Dodger Stadium on Thursday, March 26.Yoshinobu Yamamoto was credited as the winning pitcher after allowing five hits, two earned runs, while striking out six in six innings of work for the Dodgers. The Diamondbacks scored their two runs in the fourth inning to take an early lead.Arizona was limited to just one more hit in the game after Yamaoto’s night was complete. The Dodgers scored four runs in both the fifth and seventh innings to secure the victory.Catcher Will Smith and centerfielder Andy Pages produced similar lines, going 2-for-4 with a home run and three RBIs apiece.Shohei Ohtani finished the game going 1-for-3 with a run scored for the Dodgers.The Dodgers and Diamondbacks will pick the series back up on Friday, March 27.USA TODAY Sports provided updates and highlights for the Dodgers' game against the Diamondbacks on Opening Day: Final: Dodgers 8, Diamondbacks 2The Dodgers retired 18 of the last 19 batters for the Diamondbacks in the victory. 8th inning: Dodgers 8, Diamondbacks 2Diamondbacks pitcher Andrew Hoffman hits Mookie Betts in the bottom of the inning, loading up the bases for the Dodgers. Freddie Freeman grounds out to first on the next at-bat to end the inning. 7th inning: Dodgers 8, Diamondbacks 2Kyle Tucker comes up big with an RBI double for his first hit as a Dodger. Shohei Ohtani originally got on base after he was hit by Taylor Clarke's pitch and brought in to score by Tucker.Mookie Betts followed it up with an RBI single on his next at-bat, allowing Tucker to score and increase the lead.The Dodgers continue to pile on against Clarke and the Diamondbacks as Will Smith hits a two-run home run that brings in Betts.Arizona makes a pitching change that removes Clarke from the game. Andrew Hoffman comes out of the bullpen for the Diamondbacks. 6th inning: Dodgers 4, Diamondbacks 2Yoshinobu Yamamoto remains in the game as the Dodgers hold the lead. Marte and Carroll both grounded out to second for the Diamondbacks. Yamamoto struck out Perdomo to get the Dodgers to the bottom of the inning.The Dodgers produced similar results as Arizona, with Hernandez grounding out, Pages hitting a pop-up to third and Miguel Rojas striking out. 5th inning: Dodgers 4, Diamondbacks 2The Dodgers take the lead after a three-run home run hit by Andy Pages. He sent the ball 400 feet to left-center field. Max Muncy and Teoscar Hernandez were brought in to score as a result of the home run off Diamondbacks pitcher Zac Gallen.Gallen allowed Miguel Rojas to single and Shohei Ohtani to walk before the Diamondbacks decided to make a pitching change.Relief pitcher Juan Morillo enters the game for Arizona. Morillo would find himself with the bases loaded in the inning with Will Smith at the plate.Smith singled and drove in Rojas to score. 4th inning: Diamondbacks 2, Dodgers 0The Diamondbacks take the first lead of the game with Geraldo Perdomo's two-run home run, which he sent 398 feet into right field. Corbin Carroll singled to right before he was brought in to score by Perdomo.The Dodgers were unable to respond in the bottom of the inning with Mookie Betts grounding out, Freddie Freeman hit a flyout to left field and Will Smith lining out to center field. 3rd inning: Dodgers 0, Diamondbacks 0The game remained scoreless through three innings of play. The Dodgers produced a double-play, getting both Ketel Marte and Jordan Lawlar out to send it to the bottom of the inning.Kyle Tucker and Miguel Rojas grounded out in the inning. Shohei Ohtani flied out to left field. 2nd inning: Dodgers 0, Diamondbacks 0The Dodgers made quick work of the Diamondbacks in the top of the second inning. Gabriel Moreno flied out to centerfield, Nolan Arenado popped out to second and Carlos Santana struck out looking against Yoshinobu Yamamoto of the Dodgers.Zac Gallen had similar success on the mound, including striking out Andy Pages to end the inning. Will Smith grounded out and Teoscar Hernandez lined out to center field. Max Muncy managed to get on base after being walked in the inning by Gallen. 1st inning: Dodgers 0, Diamondbacks 0Pitcher Yoshinobu Yamamoto and the Dodgers managed to get out of the top of the inning after just four batters. The top of the inning concluded after Geraldo Perdomo was caught stealing second base. He had previously singled to right field to initially get on base.Shohei Ohtani managed to get the Dodgers' offense started early with a single of his own to right field against Diamondbacks pitcher Zac Gallen. Kyle Tucker made his regular-season debut as a Dodger in the first inning but grounded out in his first at-bat. Ohtani was also out at second base. Mookie Betts struck out swinging and Freddie Freeman also grounded out to first to end the inning. How to watch Dodgers vs. DiamondbacksWhen: Thursday, March 26, 5:30 p.m. PT (8:30 p.m. ET)Where: Dodger Stadium (Los Angeles)TV: NBCStreaming: Peacock, Fubo Shohei Ohtani provides a gift for Dodgers teammatesShohei Ohtani presented his Dodgers teammates with a $4,000 Seiko watch, according to ESPN's Alden Gonzalez. Clayton Kershaw's new roleFormer Dodgers pitcher Clayton Kershaw was back at Dodger Stadium for the season opener on Thursday.Kershaw served as a member of NBC's pregame broadcast in a shirt and a sports coat near the dugout. In the final segment before the game began, he spoke highly of Dodgers starting pitcher Yoshinobu Yamamoto.Kershaw spent his entire 18-year career with the Dodgers before retiring after the franchise won back-to-back titles in 2025. Magic Johnson throws out first pitchLos Angeles Lakers legend Magic Johnson threw out the ceremonial first pitch to Shohei Ohtani before the Dodgers' season opener against the Diamondbacks.Johnson is a member of Guggenheim Baseball Management, the ownership group for the Dodgers. Dave Roberts believes this is Dodgers best team on paperDodgers manager Dave Roberts spoke to NBC broadcaster Bob Costas before the season opener and spoke highly about the roster.\"On paper, this is the best team we have had,\" Roberts said. \"In 2021, we had a talented roster and came up short.\"On paper (with) the starting pitchers, the position players depth, the experience and the youth. It's the best team we've had on paper, but you've got to play the games.\" Dodgers continue to celebrate back-to-back championshipsFreddie Freeman and Miguel Rojas arrived on the field in a lowrider along with actor Will Ferrell with the championship trophies. Freeman was carrying the 2024 World Series Trophy. Rojas was holding the 2025 trophy.The Dodgers ownership group, which includes Mark Walter, raised the championship flag in the center field plaza.Former Dodgers pitcher Steve Garvey and Spanish broadcaster Jaime Jarrin were also on hand to unveil the championship sign that read \"2025\" in right field.Dodgers vs. Diamondbacks odds and betting lineThe Los Angeles Dodgers are favorites to beat the Arizona Diamondbacks, according to BetMGM odds as of Thursday, March 26.Spread: Dodgers (-1.5)Moneyline: Dodgers (-275); Diamondbacks (+220)O/U: 110Dodgers starting lineup:DH: Shohei OhtaniRF: Kyle TuckerSS: Mookie Betts1B: Freddie FreemanC: Will Smith3B: Max MuncyLF: Teoscar HernandezCF: Andy Pages2B: Miguel RojasP: Yoshinobu Yamamoto Diamondbacks starting lineup:2B - Ketel MarteRF - Corbin CarrollSS - Geraldo PerdomoC - Gabriel Moreno3B - Nolan Arenado1B - Carlos SantanaLF - Jordan LawlarCF - Alek ThomasDH - Tim TawaSP - Zac Galle Diamondbacks injury report:Pavin Smith - OUT (elbow soreness)",
